%N A010030 Irregular triangle read by rows: T(n,k) (n >= 1, 0 <= k <= [n/2]) =  number of permutations of 1..n with [n/2]-k runs of consecutive pairs up and down (divided by 2).
%D A010030 F. N. David, M. G. Kendall and D. E. Barton, Symmetric Function and Allied Tables, Cambridge, 1966, p. 264.
%H A010030 Seiichi Manyama, <a href="/A010030/b010030.txt">Rows n = 1..150, flattened</a>
%F A010030 G.f. for number of permutations of 1..n by number of runs of consecutive pairs up and down is Sum_{n>=0} n! * ( ((1-y)*(2*x^2-x^3)-x)/((1-y)*x^2-1) )^n, cf. A010029. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Nov 23 2007
